# Passkeys frontend TODO

Generated by the light-it auth package. This layer covers the passkey services
and the account page where a signed-in user adds a passkey, sees the list with
each name and creation date, renames one and deletes one. Passkey sign-in is
not part of this layer yet. Delete this file once you've read it.

## Files written

| File | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| `src/services/auth/passkeys/types.ts` | `Passkey`, the payload types and `getPasskeyFailure`, which maps a WebAuthn or API error to a known reason |
| `src/services/auth/passkeys/schemas.ts` | The `Passkey` response schema and the add, rename and delete form schemas |
| `src/services/auth/passkeys/api.ts` | `getPasskeys`, `addPasskey` (options, `startRegistration`, store), `renamePasskey`, `deletePasskey`, all on the shared `api` from `@/config/api` |
| `src/services/auth/passkeys/actions.ts` | `usePasskeys` and the add, rename and delete mutations, which refresh the list |
| `src/routes/_private/account/passkeys/page.tsx` | `/account/passkeys`: the list, "Add passkey", rename and delete |
| `src/routes/_private/account/passkeys/-components/add-passkey-dialog.tsx` | Name and password, then the browser's passkey prompt |
| `src/routes/_private/account/passkeys/-components/rename-passkey-dialog.tsx` | New name |
| `src/routes/_private/account/passkeys/-components/delete-passkey-dialog.tsx` | Password confirmation |
| `src/routes/_private/account/passkeys/-hooks/use-passkey-errors.ts` | Turns a known failure into a toast, anything else into field errors or `common.requestError` |

The TanStack Router plugin adds the route to `src/routeTree.gen.ts` the next time
`vite` runs (`dev` or `build`). Type-check after that.

## How it works

1. Every call uses the cookie session through the shared `api`; there is no token.
2. Add: the password goes to `POST passkeys/registration-options`, which returns the
   WebAuthn creation options. `startRegistration` from `@simplewebauthn/browser` runs
   `navigator.credentials.create` with them and returns the credential as JSON,
   which goes with the name to `POST passkeys`. The backend spends the challenge on
   that call, so a second submit starts over from the password.
3. A wrong password is a `422` on the `password` field and shows under it.
4. A cancelled or timed-out browser prompt, a device that can't create passkeys, a
   site address that doesn't match `PASSKEYS_RP_ID`, a device that already holds a
   passkey for the account, an expired challenge (`410`) and a failed verification
   (`422` `passkey_registration_failed`) each get their own message. Any other
   failure shows `common.requestError`.
5. Rename and delete refresh the list. Delete asks for the password again.
6. When the browser has no WebAuthn support the page says so instead of offering
   "Add passkey".

`@simplewebauthn/browser` turns the base64url JSON the backend sends into the
`ArrayBuffer`s the WebAuthn API wants and back, with no dependencies of its own.

## i18n keys

`src/i18n/locales/en.json` is not edited for you. Add this block at the top level:

```json
"passkeys": {
  "title": "Passkeys",
  "description": "Passkeys let you sign in with your fingerprint, face or screen lock instead of a password.",
  "loading": "Loading your passkeys...",
  "loadError": "We couldn't load your passkeys. Reload the page to retry.",
  "empty": "You haven't added a passkey yet.",
  "createdAt": "Added {date}",
  "form": {
    "name": "Passkey name",
    "nameTooLong": "Use 100 characters or fewer."
  },
  "add": {
    "open": "Add passkey",
    "title": "Add a passkey",
    "description": "Name it after the device it lives on, then confirm with your password.",
    "submit": "Continue",
    "success": "Passkey added"
  },
  "rename": {
    "open": "Rename",
    "title": "Rename passkey",
    "description": "Pick a name that tells you which device this passkey is on.",
    "submit": "Save",
    "success": "Passkey renamed"
  },
  "delete": {
    "open": "Delete",
    "title": "Delete passkey",
    "description": "Enter your password to delete {name}. You won't be able to use it again.",
    "submit": "Delete",
    "success": "{name} was deleted"
  },
  "errors": {
    "cancelled": "The passkey request was cancelled or timed out.",
    "unsupported": "This browser or device can't create passkeys.",
    "invalidDomain": "Passkeys aren't set up for this site's address.",
    "alreadyRegistered": "This device already has a passkey for your account.",
    "challengeExpired": "The request expired. Try again.",
    "verificationFailed": "We couldn't verify the passkey. Try again."
  }
}
```

Only if you add the sidebar link below, add `passkeys` next to the existing
`navigation.links` keys:

```json
"navigation": { "links": { "passkeys": "Passkeys" } }
```

The screens also reuse `form.password`, `form.errors.required`, `buttons.cancel`
and `common.requestError`, which the boilerplate already has.

### Optional: link the page from the sidebar

The package does not edit your navigation. To add a link, in
`src/routes/_private/-components/sidebar/sidebar.tsx` add this entry at the end of
the `links` array:

```tsx
{ path: "/account/passkeys", label: t("navigation.links.passkeys"), icon: <Icons.Lock /> },
```

